react-native-webview 14.0.1 for Android Gradle Plugin 9 with built-in Kotlin and the new DSL.

Its build file applies the `kotlin-android` plugin itself, which AGP 9 refuses when it provides Kotlin ("Cannot add extension with name 'kotlin'"), and sets
the SDK with the old `compileSdkVersion` call, which the new DSL does not have. With this the application does not need the two opt-outs
`android.builtInKotlin=false` and `android.newDsl=false`, which AGP 10 removes. The same helper is in op-sqlite's build file.

Applied by scripts/apply-patches.cjs after an install. Remove it when react-native-webview does this itself (newer than 14.0.1).

